    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0567" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg533"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Depuy de Lôme to
                        Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lenox,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1897-09-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 2,
                    1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Continuing the work undertaken in
                    order to remove from the shores of the United States a hostile expedition
                    against a Spanish province, which work has, for some weeks past, given rise to
                    various notifications from this legation, a large number of Cubans left Tampa
                    last Saturday for Cleveland by special train, this point being about 6 miles
                    from Punta Gorda, Fla., where they embarked, if my information is correct, on
                    board of the schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Cherub</hi>, from Key West.</p>
                <p>The movements of certain well-known filibustering agents at Miami, Fla., and at
                    Cape Florida lead me to suspect that the members of the Tampa expedition are on
                    one of the keys near the points which I have mentioned, and I therefore beg your
                    excellency to consider whether it would be proper for a revenue cutter to watch
                    and search those keys in order to prevent the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dauntless</hi>, in one of the false sorties which she is making, from
                    taking them on board, as is doubtless her intention, and conveying them to the
                    place where they probably expect to receive the arms shipped by the schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Donna F. Briggs</hi>.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Dupuy de Lôme</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
